\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \small  Asymptotic slopes of $-\ln \lambda _{\min }=s\mu +b$, uniformized at $\mu =30$--$38$: $s$ is the secant slope over the two segments ending at $\mu \approx 30$ and $\mu \approx 38$, whose agreement ($\pm 2\%$ typical) is the stationarity criterion. $D=\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{p\mid q}\log p/(\sqrt  p-1)$ is the prime mass removed from the window by the conductor. Intercepts $b$ are not yet uniformized across the family ($b_\zeta \approx -20$) and are omitted. $\dagger $~$\chi _{15}$ is still transient at $\mu =38$: its lower bound is excluded from the asymptotic slopes and from the fit, and its settling scale is not yet bracketed.}}{3}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
